#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:173
msgid ""
"``typsphinx-init`` is a show function that registers ``codly-languages`` "
"as codly's language table for the content it wraps, through ``show: codly"
".lang-set_(languages: codly-languages)``. It sets no other codly field "
"and installs no rule that turns raw blocks into codly blocks: typsphinx "
"emits every code block as an explicit ``codly.new(raw(...))`` call, and a"
" raw block you write yourself (in a template or a ``.. raw:: typst`` "
"directive) is left to Typst's own rendering -- wrap it in "
"``codly.new(...)`` to render it through codly. Imported names and top-"
"level show rules do not cross ``#include()``, so every content file and "
"every wrapper imports ``deps.typ`` and applies ``#show: typsphinx-init`` "
"itself. A template does not need to apply ``typsphinx-init``; the wrapper"
" already does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:186
msgid ""
"**Migrating from codly 1.3.** Earlier releases imported codly 1.3.0 with "
"``*`` and exported ``codly-init`` and the state-style ``codly`` "
"configuration function. Both are gone. A template that used them changes "
"as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:191
msgid "Remove ``#show: codly-init.with()`` -- codly 2.0 needs no initialisation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:193
msgid ""
"Replace a state-style ``codly`` configuration call with a scoped show "
"rule, ``#show: codly.set_(...)``, or pass the fields to one block, "
"``#codly.new(raw(...), ...)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:196
msgid ""
"A ``typst_dependencies`` file must import codly as a module, ``#import "
"\"@preview/codly:2.0.0\" as codly``, because the generated markup calls "
"``codly.new``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:200
msgid ""
"**Take package names from deps.typ, do not pin versions.** A template "
"that needs one of these functions imports it from the shared file instead"
" of pinning its own ``@preview/`` version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:209
msgid ""
"A template that pins its own version loads a second copy of the package "
"next to the one the generated markup uses: Typst has no version "
"resolution, so both load side by side with no error, and the document "
"mixes two versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:214
msgid ""
"**Drift warning.** typsphinx scans every ``.typ`` file of each used "
"template bundle after copying it. When a file pins one of the five "
"packages at a version different from the effective ``deps.typ``, the "
"build prints one warning per file and package, and still succeeds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:223
msgid ""
"The warning is a best-effort aid, not a guarantee. It reads literal "
"``@preview/<package>:<version>`` text with comments removed, so it cannot"
" see an import string built at run time or an import reached through a "
"file outside the bundle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/templates.rst:228
msgid ""
"**Replacing deps.typ.** The ``typst_dependencies`` configuration value "
"(see :doc:`configuration`) replaces the generated file with your own, "
"copied verbatim. Only the default versions in the table above are "
"supported. The translator emits calls written against the APIs of those "
"default versions, so output built with a replaced ``deps.typ`` is not "
"guaranteed to compile or to render correctly; a replaced file is used at "
"your own risk. A replaced file must still export every name in the table "
"above."
msgstr ""

